From 22d559805c9ebd3333424bd5aba93dc69ffd7627 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Mike Kinney <mike.kinney@gmail.com>
Date: Sun, 8 Nov 2026 15:27:02 -0800
Subject: [PATCH] fix(post): Fanuc probe result folds the expected value's sign
 into the operator

An edge or outside-corner probe whose expected value is negative in the
work offset wrote a doubled sign: `#190=#100--17` for the deviation and
`IF[ABS[#5061--12]LT0.001]` for the no-contact check. Both now go through
one helper, minusU, which folds the sign into the operator (`#100+17`) and
writes no term for a value that formats to zero (`#190=#100`). Output stays
in the unbracketed macro B form `#i=#j+#k`; the bore-centre golden is
unchanged.

Pinned by edge_probe_at_negative_x_folds_the_sign,
corner_probe_at_negative_xy_folds_both_signs and
edge_probe_at_zero_writes_the_bare_mean (fanuc_post), with new goldens
nc/fanuc/probe_edge_negative_x.nc and probe_corner_negative.nc; every
posted line is checked for `--`, `+-` and `-+`.

Fixes #377

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
